A public way to forget one path's copy in `srcToStore`.

`fetchToStore2` (src/libfetchers/fetch-to-store.cc) keeps each source
path's store copy in `fetchers::Settings::srcToStore`, and reads it
before it copies. So after an edit, `"${./x}"` names the old copy for
as long as the settings live. huggorm's `forget_file` makes the next
evaluation read an edited file, and it cannot erase the entry: the
header only forward-declares `SrcToStore` (nixidae/nixidae#997).
Measured on 2.35 and 2.36pre: after an edit and `forget_file`, the
interpolation still gave the old store path.

2.34 keeps the map on `EvalState`, which huggorm reaches directly.

diff -ruN a/src/libfetchers/fetch-to-store.cc b/src/libfetchers/fetch-to-store.cc
--- a/src/libfetchers/fetch-to-store.cc	2026-10-21 11:39:49.628063906 +0200
+++ b/src/libfetchers/fetch-to-store.cc	2026-10-21 11:39:56.152104469 +0200
@@ -20,6 +20,11 @@
     return make_ref<SrcToStore>();
 }
 
+void fetchers::Settings::forgetSrcToStore(const SourcePath & path) const
+{
+    srcToStore->cache.erase_if([&](const auto & entry) { return std::get<0>(entry.first) == path; });
+}
